Subject: Let the platform draw the text context menu

Upstream leaves this empty on the Kotlin/Native targets:

    internal actual fun ProvideDefaultPlatformTextContextMenuProviders(...) {
        // TODO: https://youtrack.jetbrains.com/issue/CMP-7819
    }

So a selection on macOS offers nothing, and what a reader gets instead is whatever
the deprecated path happens to draw. Filled in here with NSMenu, which is the menu
the reader already knows: the same keys, the same dismissal, read by a screen
reader, and looking like the rest of the machine.

Two things were found while filling it in and are fixed with it.

Both macOS text field paths returned their Modifier unchanged from
addBasicTextFieldTextContextMenuComponents, so Cut, Copy, Paste and Select All
were not absent from the menu, they were never built. The entries and their
labels are shared with Linux through a new nativeMain file.

isCopyKeyEvent was TODO("implement native isCopyKeyEvent"), which throws. Copying
with the keyboard out of a SelectionContainer crashed.

Linux keeps an empty provider: it has the entries now, and nothing to draw them
with until it has a menu of its own.
--
